From e2b242cb83bb0fb0766d5c903f739f6917b5f21d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitriy Andreychenko <dmitriy.andreychenko@flant.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 14:07:11 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] ces: give a shared pod address a single owner

DVP live-migrates a VM as two pods on two nodes holding one IPv4. The
network.deckhouse.io/pod-common-ip-priority label picks the owner: the operator
publishes the address on that CiliumEndpoint only, and the other node withholds
its cilium_lxc entry until the address returns.

Folds in 007: a departing CiliumEndpoint no longer updates ipcache for an
address it does not own, and a dead local endpoint is not restored from a stale
CiliumEndpointSlice.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
